Third-Party Notice: MITK-Diffusion (Fiberfox)
=============================================

TRXScan is an independent Rust reimplementation of the diffusion-MRI simulation
pipeline known as Fiberfox, part of MITK-Diffusion
(https://github.com/MIC-DKFZ/MITK-Diffusion), developed by the German Cancer
Research Center (DKFZ), Division of Medical Image Computing. TRXScan's simulation
physics is ported — largely function by function — from that source, which we
gratefully acknowledge as the reference implementation.

The Fiberfox method is described in:

  Neher PF, Laun FB, Stieltjes B, Maier-Hein KH. "Fiberfox: Facilitating the
  creation of realistic white matter software phantoms." Magnetic Resonance in
  Medicine. 2014;72(5):1460-1470.

Files in TRXScan that contain MITK-Diffusion-derived code (each module's doc
comment carries the specific file:line anchors into the MITK source):

  - src/raster.rs        segment/voxel intersection (itkTractsToDWIImageFilter.cpp, IntersectImage)
  - src/signal.rs        Stick / Tensor / Ball signal models (SignalModels/*)
  - src/compartments.rs  signal accumulation + normalization (itkTractsToDWIImageFilter.cpp)
  - src/scheme.rs        Fiberfox gradient encoding (mitkStickModel.cpp)
  - src/readout.rs       single-shot EPI trajectory + timing (mitkSingleShotEpi.h)
  - src/kspace.rs        k-space acquisition (itkKspaceImageFilter.cpp)
  - src/motion.rs        head-motion simulation (itkTractsToDWIImageFilter.cpp, SimulateMotion)
  - src/mat.rs           rotation-matrix helpers (mitkDiffusionImageHelperFunctions.h)

